Author: kunchenguid <[redacted email]>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 17:41:54 2026 -0700

    fix: one answer owner per question, carried onto the crew report turn

    The captain saw the same "PR 58 is merged" answer on two cards. Both came
    from the same crewmate: emit_card hands the model back the resolved card
    id, the crewmate resent it to revise its card in place, and the crewmate
    resolver prefixed it a second time - minting a duplicate instead of a
    revision. resolveFirstmateCardId already guarded against exactly this;
    the crewmate path did not.

    Three layers, so the duplicate cannot come back by another route:

    - The crewmate id resolver is idempotent, like the Firstmate one, so a
      resent id revises the open card.
    - Answer ownership is carried onto the crewmate's own report turn when
      that crewmate already has a card on the captain's screen, instead of
      being cleared by every operational wake. A report with nothing on
      screen leaves the turn unowned, so a silent or failed task still gets a
      Firstmate answer, and a decision naming the reporting task is still
      allowed when the crew showed none - that card is the captain's control
      surface, not a restatement.
    - Firstmate is told, both as a standing rule and inside the report wake
      itself, that the crew's card is already on screen and the report is
      for it to act on, not to relay. The gate refuses a repeat; the
      instruction stops it reaching for one.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

